// PatchInstructions sets instrumentation points and patches to be applied in a module.
//
// Mark that all instrumentation points matching instructionId are to be
// patched in order to call the device function identified by
// deviceCallbackName. It is up to the API client to ensure that this
// device callback exists and match the correct callback format for
// this instrumentation point.
// [AddPatchesFromFile], [AddPatches], [PatchInstructions],
// and [PatchModule]. For example if [AddPatches](fileName) and
// sanitizerPatchInstruction(*, *, cbName) are called concurrently and cbName
// is intended to be found in the loaded module, the results are undefined.
//
//   - instructionId: Instrumentation point for which to insert patches
//   - module: CUDA module to instrument
//   - deviceCallbackName: Name of the device function callback that the inserted patch will call at the instrumented points. This function is expected to be found in code previously loaded by [AddPatchesFromFile] or [AddPatches]
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: if unable to initialize the sanitizer.
//   - [ErrInvalidParameter]: if module is not a CUDA module or if deviceCallbackName function cannot be located.
//
// Wraps sanitizerPatchInstructions.
func PatchInstructions(instructionId InstructionId, module Module, deviceCallbackName string) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("sanitizerPatchInstructions"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	deviceCallbackName_cstr := append([]byte(deviceCallbackName), 0)
	return toError(fnPatchInstructions(instructionId, module, &deviceCallbackName_cstr[0]), "sanitizerPatchInstructions")
}

